00:22:18,021 --> 00:22:20,619
最终并不是支撑线或阻力线。
that ultimately makes a market go up or down.

442
00:22:20,620 --> 00:22:26,340
真正推动市场上涨或下跌的，是支撑和阻力背后的原理。
It's the underlying principles around that support and resistance that make the market go up and down.

445
00:22:29,160 --> 00:22:37,140
比如，主动交易推动市场激进上涨，而响应交易显示大量流动性被使用。
For example, initiative makes the market go up aggressively. Responsive shows us a high amount of liquidity being utilized.

447
00:22:37,560 --> 00:22:43,480
平衡市场往往难以突破，不平衡市场则提供良好的突破机会。
Balanced markets tend to struggle to break out. Imbalanced markets show us good breakout opportunities.

449
00:22:44,120 --> 00:22:46,265
现在，掌握这些基本原理后，你不仅能采用我教的策略，还能最终学会自己捕鱼。
Now, knowing these basic principles, ultimately,

450
00:22:46,265 --> 00:22:49,840
not only can you adopt the strategies I'm showing you,

451
00:22:49,840 --> 00:22:53,773
But you can ultimately then learn to catch your own fish.

452
00:22:54,140 --> 00:22:55,760
这就是本课程的目的。
And that's the purpose of this course.

453
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:58,300
目的是我来教你这些原理。
The purpose is for me to teach you the principles.

454
00:22:58,300 --> 00:23:01,975
为你提供一个习惯化流程，每天学习并应用这些原理，希望你不仅能采用我的策略，还能开发自己的策略。
Give you a habitual process for learning and adopting those principles

455
00:23:01,975 --> 00:23:06,318
every single day, in hopes that not only do you adopt my strategies,

456
00:23:06,318 --> 00:23:07,656
but learn your own.

458
00:23:09,260 --> 00:23:10,460
现在开始讲解。
Let's get into that now.

459
00:23:10,540 --> 00:23:15,360
我们来讨论拍卖不平衡中的这些原理。
Let's talk about those principles that you're going to find within the auction imbalance.

461
00:23:17,880 --> 00:23:19,440
强和弱的拍卖过程。
So, strong and weak auction processes.

462
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:24,880
我认为最好的开始方式，是再画一个小的不平衡图。
Now, again, I think the best way to start is to just draw a little bit of an imbalance again.

464
00:23:25,720 --> 00:23:28,660
我们来画10和100。
So, let's go 10 and 100.

465
00:23:29,280 --> 00:23:35,700
我只在这里画顶部的，20，我要画得非常非常——几乎可笑。
I'm just going to draw the top ones here, 20. I'm going to make it really, really—almost silly.

467
00:23:36,640 --> 00:23:39,280
30和100，还有40。
30 and 100 and 40.

468
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:45,340
显然，我们能看到这些不平衡。
So, we can see, obviously, the imbalances.

469
00:23:45,540 --> 00:23:46,200
哦，回到之前。
Oh, let's go back.

470
00:23:46,460 --> 00:23:48,260
你能看到那里的不平衡。
So, you can see the imbalances there.

471
00:23:48,640 --> 00:23:51,260
我不想花太多时间画不平衡。
I don't want to spend too much time drawing out imbalances.

472
00:23:56,680 --> 00:23:57,980
好的，所以存在不平衡。
Alright. So, there are imbalances.

473
00:23:58,420 --> 00:24:03,340
现在，最关键的是要解读强和弱的拍卖过程。
Now, ultimately, the first thing to interpret is a strong and weak auction process.

475
00:24:05,080 --> 00:24:09,100
理论上，拍卖不平衡是强拍卖过程。
An auction imbalance is, in theory, a strong auction process.

476
00:24:10,920 --> 00:24:16,994
然而，这才是理解这个策略最重要的一点，只有当不平衡推动深色块时，才是强拍卖过程。
However, and this is the most important thing to understanding this strategy,

477
00:24:16,994 --> 00:24:23,576
It's only a strong auction process if the imbalance is lifting dark colors.

479
00:24:26,320 --> 00:24:27,440
这是真正的关键。
This is the real key.

480
00:24:27,620 --> 00:24:29,760
如果你在不平衡形成时看到真正的深色块，
If you have some real dark colors

481
00:24:29,760 --> 00:24:32,900
你会看到一些真正的深色阴影，
as the imbalance is created, you’re getting some real dark shades

483
00:24:34,300 --> 00:24:35,100
随着价格上涨。
as we go up.

484
00:24:35,680 --> 00:24:37,420
换句话说，真正的卖盘正在被吃掉。
In other words, real offers are being lifted.

485
00:24:37,780 --> 00:24:41,220
买方极其主动，正在吃掉大量成交量。
The buyer is being that aggressive and is lifting very high amounts of volume.

487
00:24:41,560 --> 00:24:44,920
这种不平衡表明拍卖过程非常强劲。
That sort of imbalance shows us a strong auction process.

488
00:24:45,600 --> 00:24:48,560
而相反的情况，就是弱拍卖过程。
Now, the counter—or the flip of that—is a weak auction process.

490
00:24:48,700 --> 00:24:55,960
比如，我们看到不平衡，但可能只有20比70。
I.e., where we have an imbalance, but, for instance, maybe it’s only 20 by 70.

492
00:24:56,680 --> 00:25:04,140
也就是说，成交量很低。或者1比6，或者20比140。
In other words, it’s low amounts of volume. Or 1 by 6, or again, 20 by 140.

494
00:25:05,080 --> 00:25:10,060
这比起成交量很高的情况，拍卖过程弱得多。
This is a far weaker auction process than, say, for example, we had much higher numbers.

496
00:25:10,060 --> 00:25:11,340
比如200、200、300这样的数字。
You have 200, 200, 300.

497
00:25:12,160 --> 00:25:13,480
我等会儿会展示这两个例子。
I’ll show those two examples in a bit.

498
00:25:13,660 --> 00:25:16,000
但你只需理解这个基本前提：强拍卖。
But just understand that basic premise: a strong auction.

499
00:25:16,060 --> 00:25:20,740
我们在对角线方向上吃掉大量成交量。
We’re lifting high amounts of volume as we’re going in the diagonal way, of course.

501
00:25:21,420 --> 00:25:22,460
弱拍卖则相反。
And a weak auction.

502
00:25:22,740 --> 00:25:25,700
同样是对角线，但我们在卖盘上吃掉的量非常小。
Again, diagonally, but we’re lifting very small amounts on the offer.

503
00:25:25,700 --> 00:25:30,600
现在，基本前提——经验法则：强拍卖不会立即反转。
Now, the basic premise—the rule of thumb: A strong auction won’t always reverse straight away.

505
00:25:30,700 --> 00:25:31,640
它很可能继续延续。
It’s likely to continue.

506
00:25:31,880 --> 00:25:33,960
弱拍卖则很可能反转。
A weak auction will likely reverse.

507
00:25:34,100 --> 00:25:36,536
我学到这个策略的地方——如果你长期交易德国国债，你会发现市场在午餐时间，中午前后会出现大量翻转。
Now, where I learned this—actually, this strategy—was

508
00:25:36,536 --> 00:25:39,784
if you’ve been a German Bund trader for a long time,

509
00:25:39,784 --> 00:25:44,115
you’ll notice that a lot of flipping comes into the market around about lunchtime, midday.

510
00:25:44,360 --> 00:25:48,920
这种翻转通常看起来像弱拍卖不平衡。
Now, this flipping very often will look like a weak auction imbalance.

512
00:25:48,920 --> 00:25:51,053
所以，如果你想学会交易这个策略，最佳交易时机之一——比如在德国国债里——就是午餐时间。
So, if you want to learn to trade this,

513
00:25:51,053 --> 00:25:54,608
one of the best times to trade this—in, say, for instance, the German Bunds—

514
00:25:54,608 --> 00:25:55,319
is around lunchtime.

515
00:25:55,400 --> 00:25:57,960
也就是欧洲时段的11点到1点。
So, 11 o’clock to 1 o’clock in the European session.

516
00:25:58,500 --> 00:26:03,360
现在，我等会儿会讲这个策略的变体。
Now, I’ll go through the variations of the strategy in a minute.

518
00:26:03,780 --> 00:26:06,220
但我们先聊聊其他原理。
But let’s just talk about some of the other principles.

519
00:26:06,340 --> 00:26:09,080
现在，失衡市场与平衡市场。
Now, imbalanced versus balanced markets.

520
00:26:09,500 --> 00:26:16,380
失衡市场——我总是说——是指失去平衡的市场。
So, an imbalanced market—again, as I always say—a market that’s out of balance.

522
00:26:16,500 --> 00:26:20,551
也就是说，我们在接近前一交易日的极值点附近交易，甚至突破极值点的任意一侧。
So, i.e., we’re trading relatively close to the previous day’s extreme,

523
00:26:20,551 --> 00:26:23,156
or even outside of the extreme on either side.

525
00:26:23,180 --> 00:26:28,400
在我看来，在这些极值点附近，你会看到更强的拍卖不平衡。
For me, you tend to see much stronger auction imbalances at those extreme points.

526
00:26:28,520 --> 00:26:30,960
我会非常谨慎地反向操作这些。
I’d be far more cautious to fade those.

527
00:26:31,240 --> 00:26:34,240
但别担心。我会给大家展示一个
But again, don’t worry. I’m going to show you an exact strategy

528
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:36,160
具体策略：如何反向、何时反向、为何反向。
of how to fade, when to fade, and why to fade.

529
00:26:36,160 --> 00:26:40,720
所以，在不平衡市场中，我们更可能看到更多不平衡。
So, in an imbalanced market, we are likely to see more of these imbalances.

531
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:47,175
而在平衡市场中，如果我们在前一交易日区间中点附近交易，更可能看到较弱类型的不平衡，正如我所说，这些不平衡往往会自行反转。
Whereas, in a balanced market, where we’re trading smack in the middle of the previous day’s range,

532
00:26:47,175 --> 00:26:52,700
we are likely to see more weaker-type imbalances, which, as I said, tend to reverse upon themselves.

536
00:26:53,260 --> 00:26:56,720
现在，注意：我提到了高成交量和低成交量。
Now, note: I’ve mentioned the high and low volume.

